== Part B: SU(2), 1^3 x 1 slab, exact
  one temporal link V; plaquette k: tr(x_k V y_k^+ V^+) = 2 (x_k0 y_k0 + x_k . R(V) y_k), |.| <= 2
  the twist flips y_k, so the weight changes by exp(-2 beta (x_k0 y_k0 + x_k . R y_k)) >= e^{-2 beta},
  with equality for every V when x_k, y_k are centre elements (+-1): the floor is attained.
  beta = 2.3: worst twist ratio = e^(-2 beta) = 0.01005, pointwise factor = tanh(beta) = 0.9801  vs sqrt 2 - 1 = 0.4142: REFUTES the pointwise side for this slab
